# A list literal beneath a disjunction in the target: the checker matches a
# struct literal to an alternative, and nothing else beneath a disjunction.
-- source.cue --
a: string
-- target.cue --
x: [int] | [string]
-- lens.cue --
v0_0: _
v1_0: {x: [1]}
-- out --
unknown
v1_0.x[0] is written beneath v1_0.x, which is a disjunction in the target schema; the checker proves a struct literal written at v1_0.x against one of its alternatives, and descends into nothing else beneath it (rule unknown-target-constraint) @ lens.cue:2:8
